{
  "schema": "loom.runtime_profile/1",
  "domain": "graph_sources",
  "revision": 1,
  "description": "Sources of the graph projection (M1 §2.3): each row says how one kind of thing the application already has becomes nodes of the one navigable graph, on demand and without writing anything to the nodes table. id: the source; prefix: its address form (also an id form of element_resolution.pack, source projection); class: the class of its nodes (graph/classes.pack); reader: the mechanism id in loom/src/graph/projection.cpp; params: what the reader reads; parent: where its nodes hang ({root}, {area: <graph entry area>} or {of: <source>}: under the nodes of that source); contain_edge: the edge kind from a node to its parent; edges: the other edges its reader emits, as documentation of the mechanism (meanings in graph_views.pack edge_kinds; the target of has_default is read from here); epistemic_default: the evidence every node carries unless its own provenance differs (evidence_by_scope: by the scope-chain level that supplied a value; evidence_by_method: by provenance.method — model_inferred is never observed); page_setting: the config key that pages a large source; same_as_prefix: the database id form of the same node (conv:<id> = c_<id>). Removing a source removes that projection and nothing else (the graph is as before). Everything is data: the user's overlay <data_dir>/profiles/graph_sources.pack may move a source to another area, change the evidence or hide a source (hidden: true). value_words: the words of the values in words (value_human) and of the chips; slot_labels: the names of the interview's slots; role_modes: which role shows a background mode (worker profile); proposals_status: why a setting has no proposal yet.",
  "defaults": {
    "schema": "loom.graph_sources/1",
    "sources": [
      {
        "id": "area",
        "prefix": "area:",
        "class": "graph_area",
        "reader": "graph_entry.areas",
        "label": {
          "en": "Areas of the graph",
          "pl": "Obszary grafu"
        },
        "parent": {
          "root": true
        },
        "contain_edge": "part_of",
        "edges": [],
        "epistemic_default": {
          "class": "declared",
          "confidence": 1.0
        },
        "description": "The root rows: the areas of the graph entry view (graph/entry.pack with the user's graph_entry overlay), each with its counters."
      },
      {
        "id": "rom",
        "prefix": "rom:",
